00:13:39,310 --> 00:13:41,690
It was the ring.

267
00:13:44,570 --> 00:13:48,570
Hey, so was he excited about the tickets?

268
00:13:44,570 --> 00:13:48,570
No. He blew us off.

269
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,700
What?

270
00:13:48,740 --> 00:13:50,700
I know.

271
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:52,780
I can't believe it.

272
00:13:53,410 --> 00:13:55,120
Can I tell you something?

273
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,910
I'm a little mad at him now.

274
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,330
Can I tell you something?

275
00:14:02,880 --> 00:14:04,380
Me too.

276
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:09,630
You know what? He didn't want to talk to us about being angry?

277
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:12,390
Well, maybe we don't talk to him at all.

278
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,640
Ooh.

279
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,600
Freeze him out.

280
00:14:15,180 --> 00:14:16,600
That's right.

281
00:14:16,770 --> 00:14:18,350
I like it.

282
00:14:16,770 --> 00:14:18,350
Ah? We'll show him.

283
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:22,270
From now on, it's gonna be Joey and Ross, best friends.

284
00:14:22,440 --> 00:14:25,780
Okay, we're gonna be the new Joey and Chandler. Ha, ha.

285
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:31,570
Hi, I'm back.

286
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:33,830
There's more to tell you. I've written it all down.

287
00:14:33,990 --> 00:14:35,910
Oh, that's great.

288
00:14:37,620 --> 00:14:40,250
No, actually, that's...

289
00:14:40,500 --> 00:14:43,040
That's great. That's really great.

290
00:14:43,210 --> 00:14:48,050
You know, I gotta tell you, writing, all that writing, it gets me, uh...

291
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:50,680
It gets me kind of hot.

292
00:14:50,840 --> 00:14:53,470
Wait, wait. Listen to this:

293
00:14:54,390 --> 00:14:57,100
Know what I wanted to be when I was that age?

294
00:14:57,600 --> 00:14:58,980
A lover?

295
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,270
A surfer.

296
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:01,270
Oh, yeah. A surfer?

297
00:15:01,850 --> 00:15:05,020
I wanted to be one with the waves...

298
00:15:01,850 --> 00:15:05,020
Honey, hold on real quick.

299
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:09,690
Hold on a second. Let me just get a little more comfortable here.

300
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,030
Wait a second.

301
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,410
This isn't too revealing, is it?

302
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:14,410
No.

303
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:17,580
Whatever happened to that little dude?

304
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:20,910
So full of dreams.

305
00:15:23,080 --> 00:15:26,750
I don't care about the little dude.

306
00:15:27,210 --> 00:15:30,210
I can't. I cannot listen to any more of this.

307
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:33,930
The only one who'd listen to this is a mental health professional.

308
00:15:34,090 --> 00:15:36,430
And that's only because they get paid $100 an hour.

309
00:15:36,600 --> 00:15:38,930
Do you know how much money I could've made listening to you?

310
00:15:39,100 --> 00:15:40,640
Two thousand dollars.

311
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:43,810
And you know when I figured that out? While you were talking.

312
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:48,820
I can't believe you're trying to stifle me, when just 14 hours ago...

313
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:52,700
we figured out that that's exactly what my mother was trying to do to me.

314
00:15:54,070 --> 00:15:55,450
I'm sorry.

315
00:15:55,620 --> 00:15:59,660
I don't mean... I didn't mean to stifle you.

316
00:15:59,830 --> 00:16:02,500
This is all just a little overwhelming.

317
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,420
Oh, Rachel.

318
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:07,380
I'm so sorry.

319
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,000
I didn't mean to overwhelm you.

320
00:16:10,170 --> 00:16:13,340
It's just that when those gates open...

321
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:17,300
it's hard to close them.

322
00:16:19,930 --> 00:16:22,230
But they are closed now. Believe me.

323
00:16:22,390 --> 00:16:26,060
I'm so glad. I'm so glad you shared.

324
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:29,400
And I'm glad that you're done.

325
00:16:31,820 --> 00:16:34,110
So, what do you say we, um...

326
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,950
I'd really like that.

327
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:38,950
Mm-hm.

328
00:16:49,380 --> 00:16:52,300
That was so good.

329
00:17:02,220 --> 00:17:04,730
Oh, oh, ugh.

330
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,690
Hey.

331
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,690
I can't believe you talked me into...

332
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:11,190
buying this stupid gumball-machine-looking ring.

333
00:17:11,360 --> 00:17:15,190
It's not a stupid gumball-machine-looking ring. It's a beautiful ring.

334
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,900
No, it's not.

335
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:18,450
When I looked at the other ring...

336
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,740
I could see Monica's face when I gave it to her...

337
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:22,450
and I could see her saying yes.

338
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:24,790
When I look at this ring, all I see is a ring.

339
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:29,540
Unless I look at it really closely, and then I can see my own eye.

340
00:17:34,170 --> 00:17:37,260
Look, this is the most important thing I'm gonna do in my life.

341
00:17:37,430 --> 00:17:39,220
I want to make sure it's perfect.

342
00:17:39,390 --> 00:17:42,810
Okay. There may be a way that we could get the other ring back.

343
00:17:42,970 --> 00:17:45,730
Because I heard the guy tell the jeweler where he was gonna propose.

344
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:48,230
So maybe we could get him to trade rings or something.

345
00:17:48,480 --> 00:17:49,900
I can't do that.

346
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:53,150
Well, you certainly can't give her that stupid gumball ring.

347
00:18:02,160 --> 00:18:03,410
There he is.

348
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,500
Okay, and he hasn't proposed yet. She has no ring on her finger.

349
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:09,540
Wow, you're good. After this, we should solve crimes.

350
00:18:09,710 --> 00:18:12,170
Yeah. Okay. Go get him.

351
00:18:12,840 --> 00:18:14,250
Oh, okay.

352
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:20,550
Excuse me, sir. Could you come with me, please? You have a phone call.

353
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:23,260
Who is it?

354
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:23,260
It is your office.

355
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,890
Do you know who at my office?

356
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:25,890
John.

357
00:18:26,060 --> 00:18:27,270
Oh, John. Great.

358
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,860
There he is.

359
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:32,860
Hi. Hi. Okay.

360
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,020
Okay, there was a mix-up at the jewelry store.

361
00:18:35,190 --> 00:18:38,570
The ring you're about to propose with was supposed to be held for me.

362
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:41,070
So I'm gonna need to have that back.

363
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:47,910
But in exchange, I'm willing to trade you this beautiful, more expensive ring.

364
00:18:50,040 --> 00:18:51,830
Wow, I would trade.

365
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:56,840
It is beautiful, but I'm gonna use this one. Now, if you'll excuse me.

366
00:18:57,010 --> 00:19:00,300
No, no. See, this is my fiancee, and her heart was set on that ring.

367
00:19:00,470 --> 00:19:02,680
You don't want to break her heart now, do you?

368
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:06,100
Yeah. Do you want to break a dying woman's heart?

369
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,220
You're dying?

370
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,440
Yeah, she's dying...

371
00:19:13,610 --> 00:19:15,980
of a cough, apparently.

372
00:19:17,860 --> 00:19:21,950
It's my dying wish to have that ring. See, if I'm not buried with that ring...

373
00:19:22,110 --> 00:19:25,200
then my spirit will wander the netherworld...

374
00:19:25,370 --> 00:19:26,700
Okay, that's enough, honey.

375
00:19:28,370 --> 00:19:30,080
Oh, I don't know.

376
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,960
Let me see the ring.

377
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:34,960
Great. Okay, here.

378
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:40,010
All right, I'll do it.

379
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:40,010
Thank you. Thank you. Thank you.

380
00:19:40,170 --> 00:19:43,380
And you are about to marry a wonderful man.

381
00:19:49,430 --> 00:19:51,680
Hey, I'm marrying a dead woman.

382
00:19:58,400 --> 00:19:59,980
Guys?

383
00:20:02,990 --> 00:20:05,030
I got something important to tell you.

384
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:07,950
Guys.

385
00:20:09,410 --> 00:20:12,080
Guys?

386
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,750
I'm gonna ask Monica to marry me.

387
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:21,300
I think we gotta end the freeze-out.

388
00:20:23,550 --> 00:20:25,380
Wait a minute. Is this for real?

389
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:27,470
Yeah. Check out the ring.

390
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:30,350
Oh, my God.

391
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:33,810
So you two are really serious?

392
00:20:35,650 --> 00:20:37,480
Yeah, pretty much.

393
00:20:38,190 --> 00:20:41,360
You're gonna get married? I mean...

394
00:20:41,860 --> 00:20:44,820
We're gonna be brothers-in-law. Come here!

395
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:49,870
And we're gonna be friends again.

396
00:20:45,860 --> 00:20:49,870
Hey.

397
00:20:50,830 --> 00:20:52,200
What?

398
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:55,540
Water under the bridge. Forget it!

399
00:20:52,370 --> 00:20:55,540
Okay.

400
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:59,340
I was gonna wait till it was official, you know, but I had to tell you guys...

401
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,840
because you're my best friends.

402
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:06,180
I think I'm gonna cry.

403
00:21:02,260 --> 00:21:06,180
Oh. No more crying.

404
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:09,300
Please, I just dumped one crybaby. I'll dump you too.

405
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:13,890
I'm gonna ask Monica to marry me.

406
00:21:14,140 --> 00:21:17,810
Oh, my God.

407
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:21,230
Oh, Chandler. You guys are gonna be so happy.

408
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:24,530
I know.

409
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:24,530
Where's all the tissues?

410
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:32,620
Check out the ring.

411
00:21:32,790 --> 00:21:35,870
Oh, nice. One-and-a-half karat, easy.

412
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,870
Hey.

413
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:38,870
Hey, Pheebs.

414
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:40,920
Chandler's gonna ask Monica to marry him.

415
00:21:41,090 --> 00:21:42,920
I know. I helped pick out the ring.

416
00:21:43,090 --> 00:21:44,630
Oh.

417
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:49,260
You told her before you told us?

418
00:21:50,100 --> 00:21:52,560
She walked in while I was looking at ring brochures.

419
00:21:52,720 --> 00:21:54,770
You can understand that, right?

420
00:21:56,480 --> 00:22:02,060
Guys?

